+\details{
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:39: trailing whitespace.
+\code{ivreg} is the high-level interface to the work-horse function \code{\link{ivreg.fit}},
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:40: trailing whitespace.
+a set of standard methods (including \code{print}, \code{summary}, \code{vcov}, \code{anova},
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:41: trailing whitespace.
+\code{hatvalues}, \code{predict}, \code{terms}, \code{model.matrix}, \code{bread},
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:42: trailing whitespace.
+\code{estfun}) is available and described on \code{\link{summary.ivreg}}.
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:43: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:44: trailing whitespace.
+Regressors and instruments for \code{ivreg} are most easily specified in a formula
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:45: trailing whitespace.
+with two parts on the right-hand side, e.g., \code{y ~ x1 + x2 | z1 + z2 + z3},
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:46: trailing whitespace.
+where \code{x1} and \code{x2} are the regressors and \code{z1},
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:47: trailing whitespace.
+\code{z2}, and \code{z3} are the instruments. Note that exogenous
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:48: trailing whitespace.
+regressors have to be included as instruments for themselves. For
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:49: trailing whitespace.
+example, if there is one exogenous regressor \code{ex} and one endogenous
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:50: trailing whitespace.
+regressor \code{en} with instrument \code{in}, the appropriate formula
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:51: trailing whitespace.
+would be \code{y ~ ex + en | ex + in}. Equivalently, this can be specified as
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:52: trailing whitespace.
+\code{y ~ ex + en | . - en + in}, i.e., by providing an update formula with a
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:53: trailing whitespace.
+\code{.} in the second part of the formula. The latter is typically more convenient,
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:54: trailing whitespace.
+if there is a large number of exogenous regressors.
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:55: trailing whitespace.
+}
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:56: trailing whitespace.
+
docs/literature/raw/exec22_riv_aer_0.txt:57: trailing whitespace.
